I always wonder, what sort of game are people thinking about when they
say they want a multiplayer form of nethack?

I suspect what people want is sort of a hybrid between MUDs and
multiplayer arcade games.  The MUDs aren't sufficiently spatial;
arcade games don't have enough nouns and verbs.

In any case, the big problem is time: synchronization and fairness.

Something I've been wondering about is if you can build a game with
weak synchronization: you only need to synchronize players that are
close enough to interact.  When they're far enough apart, they can act
asynchronously.
